# Obsidian Vault Content Conventions

## Frontmatter

- YAML block delimited by `---`
- Only include properties that will be queried -- no blank or placeholder values
- Use Templater `<% %>` syntax for dynamic prompts in templates

### Optional wikilink fields (avoid blank `[[]]`)

When a relationship field is optional, do NOT write `customer: "[[<% tp.system.prompt(...) %>]]"` -- if the user submits an empty answer it produces a literal `"[[]]"` broken link. Use a Templater execution block at the top of the template, build the line conditionally, and inject it:

```javascript
<%*
const customer = await tp.system.prompt("Customer (blank for none)");
const customerLine = customer ? `customer: "[[${customer}]]"\n` : "";
-%>
---
type: meeting
date: <% tp.date.now("YYYY-MM-DD") %>
<% customerLine -%>status: active
---
```

The trailing `-%>` strips the newline after each Templater tag so the generated YAML stays compact. Required fields can stay inline (`customer: "[[<% prompt %>]]"`) -- this pattern only applies when blank is a valid answer.

## Relationship Fields

Use wikilinks, not plain text slugs. This creates backlinks:

```yaml
customer: "[[Acme Corp]]"     # Good -- creates backlink
customer: acme-corp            # Bad -- no backlink, fragile
```

## Aliases

YAML list format only:

```yaml
aliases:
  - Acme
  - ACME Corp
```

## File Naming

- Evergreen notes: Title Case with spaces (`Acme Corp.md`)
- Dated notes: `YYYY-MM-DD - Title.md`

## Tags

Cross-cutting themes only: `#security`, `#observability`, `#search`, `#migration`. Never duplicate frontmatter. Flat namespace -- no nesting.

## Dataview Queries

- Always scope to folder: `FROM "03-Meetings"`
- Use DQL, not JavaScript queries
- Add `LIMIT` on list queries
- Use `SORT` for deterministic order

## Bases

`.base` files in `content/bases/` (copied to the vault's `Bases/` folder) provide standalone interactive views. Use Bases when you want a dedicated, filterable, sortable table that lives outside any single note. Use Dataview when the table is a section of a hub page.

`.base` syntax:
- `filters:` `and:` / `or:` / `not:` with expressions like `note.type == "system"` or `file.inFolder("01-Customers")`
- `views:` array, each with `type` (table | cards | list | map), `name`, optional `filters`, `order`, `groupBy`, `limit`
- `properties:` to set display names for frontmatter fields

## Tasks Plugin

Use Tasks-plugin emoji syntax for due dates and priorities, not legacy Dataview inline fields:

```markdown
- [ ] Send proposal 📅 2026-03-14 ⏫
```

Queries on Home, daily, and weekly review templates use ```tasks blocks (Tasks-plugin syntax), not ```dataview TASK blocks.

## Diagrams

Excalidraw is primary. Embed pattern:

```markdown
![[<Note Title> - <Diagram Topic>.excalidraw]]
```

Drawings live in `Assets/Excalidraw/`. The `system`, `project`, and `customer` templates already ship with this embed placeholder. A Templater file-title interpolation looks like `![[<% tp.file.title %> - Architecture.excalidraw]]`.

Mermaid blocks are allowed only for trivial inline diagrams; never replace an Excalidraw embed with a fabricated Mermaid diagram during polish.

## Links

Wikilinks `[[Note Title]]` for all internal references. Shortest path format.

## Headings

- Every template starts with `# <% tp.file.title %>` for reading mode
- Body sections use H2 and below
- No skipped heading levels (H2 -> H3, never H2 -> H4)

## One Note, One Purpose

Each template produces one atomic note. Never combine multiple meetings or topics.
